_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/fadc28f49459b22505bc6ceb6a70fc18a38f1625/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:16:36Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:16:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add better-near-auth/react hooks and typed near atoms (#78)\n\n* feat: add better-near-auth/react hooks and typed near atoms\n\n- New `better-near-auth/react` entry: useNearState, useNearAccountId\n  (live connection with session fallback), useWalletConnected,\n  useActiveNetwork, and useNearConnection built on useSyncExternalStore\n- Export NearState, NearNetwork, NearClientAtoms, and getNearAtoms from\n  better-near-auth/client for typed vanilla access to siwnClient atoms\n- React is an optional peer dependency; no new runtime dependencies\n- Replace non-reactive render-time getAccountId() reads in the example\n  with a router-context-bound hook (app-owned lib/near.ts)\n- Update client/tanstack skills and add changeset\n\n* refactor: share readSessionNearAccountId from store.ts; drop any from atom source typing\n\n- readSessionNearAccountId(session) centralizes the session-fallback narrowing\n  (session.user.nearAccount is populated by an after-hook, so it is absent from\n  the inferred session type) — react.ts now uses it, and it is exported for\n  client.ts to adopt when rebased onto the session-fallback PR\n- NearAtomsSource and getNearAtoms drop WritableAtom<any> in favor of\n  WritableAtom<unknown> with a single guarded cast at the boundary\n- store.test.ts: cover readSessionNearAccountId, drop any from the test double\n\n* docs: client skill frontmatter advertises react hooks; document readSessionNearAccountId","tree":{"sha":"087016336b14840916239049081d30826872124f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/trees/087016336b14840916239049081d30826872124f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/commits/fadc28f49459b22505bc6ceb6a70fc18a38f1625","verification":{"payload":"tree 087016336b14840916239049081d30826872124f\nparent 442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1788401796 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788401796 -0500\n\nfeat: add better-near-auth/react hooks and typed near atoms (#78)\n\n* feat: add better-near-auth/react hooks and typed near atoms\n\n- New `better-near-auth/react` entry: useNearState, useNearAccountId\n  (live connection with session fallback), useWalletConnected,\n  useActiveNetwork, and useNearConnection built on useSyncExternalStore\n- Export NearState, NearNetwork, NearClientAtoms, and getNearAtoms from\n  better-near-auth/client for typed vanilla access to siwnClient atoms\n- React is an optional peer dependency; no new runtime dependencies\n- Replace non-reactive render-time getAccountId() reads in the example\n  with a router-context-bound hook (app-owned lib/near.ts)\n- Update client/tanstack skills and add changeset\n\n* refactor: share readSessionNearAccountId from store.ts; drop any from atom source typing\n\n- readSessionNearAccountId(session) centralizes the session-fallback narrowing\n  (session.user.nearAccount is populated by an after-hook, so it is absent from\n  the inferred session type) — react.ts now uses it, and it is exported for\n  client.ts to adopt when rebased onto the session-fallback PR\n- NearAtomsSource and getNearAtoms drop WritableAtom<any> in favor of\n  WritableAtom<unknown> with a single guarded cast at the boundary\n- store.test.ts: cover readSessionNearAccountId, drop any from the test double\n\n* docs: client skill frontmatter advertises react hooks; document readSessionNearAccountId","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmNiECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAdQQABagqboFu7z8H4Ta1p0sRCyf\n+DtfM4THnaovixIzvTpzSRRBT63prOgtNL5HKQIBdXTKG34UtkDhQQtjlPUA3LxD\nuwPAj2Fu5LxmomZZld9mfHaG68NkI4/p/YJb292ZR7EIoL/+ZNMgib12HodEWq8H\n6fF+2n4DacPbo+SZwIj+ESk2QTmphJuQRFw6aOTYO01NO8sO9lnGE15lYJsEEX7i\njdn60zGiNyRuM3fM83lE76SOJ/s+pWu3qvpBSqRbpL/T8fRd3vwGF0305A4Td7a9\nQC2u+Ahd4X9PcZsFDWlaThjbvpI15okW0RKJyn/wY56F35I/b0l/QfrIoxTfneE1\nWpX2ADPLtRl9w58cxpqFGFopSEKmkf78x1Ctb/Vls81IZeYcIgfpOaDMc91+ET6y\n1us1FzfNNgpMjkvX0U6MFT73vcP03zt5tb+WseOX3Q8qpeH7y+4JHXopsHV+LBnG\n6riasM2Yuw7h9i/ktJIGKnyx8Y1Xeiiyw+iTuM5OjfE1qEIrE4akUa48lsfVLnJm\nGTLK+wz9OHEzTpCpd33qAk+TOgG3S/RzhvuA0ZumWvP5RmR4Wt1BNLTfjTJBXoqa\nEFdxVjEeVWifDBnUMYScXOz8VU4mY/escIr0CnZ71rOm0l/sJCBdTWVS0np962cI\nNbsbGwAzSI3DInYDctwL\n=T30U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T02:16:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commit/fadc28f49459b22505bc6ceb6a70fc18a38f1625","node_id":"C_kwDOPe0UwtoAKGZhZGMyOGY0OTQ1OWIyMjUwNWJjNmNlYjZhNzBmYzE4YTM4ZjE2MjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commit/442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54","sha":"442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54"}],"sha":"fadc28f49459b22505bc6ceb6a70fc18a38f1625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/fadc28f49459b22505bc6ceb6a70fc18a38f1625"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:01:54Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:01:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: accept ml-dsa-65 NEP-413 signatures in SIWN verify endpoints (#77)\n\n* upgrade\n\n* feat: accept ml-dsa-65 NEP-413 signatures in SIWN verify endpoints\n\nWallets holding post-quantum ml-dsa-65: (FIPS 204) full-access keys are\nnow accepted by /api/auth/near/verify and /api/auth/near/link-account.\nPreviously the request bounced with 401 Unauthorized: Invalid signature\nbecause near-kit''s verifyNep413Signature hardcodes Ed25519.\n\nAdds a sibling verifyMlDsa65Nep413Signature helper that uses\n@noble/post-quantum''s ml_dsa65.verify, re-using the same NEP-413\nSHA-256 + borsh payload format and the same timestamp-based maxAge\ncheck. The ml-dsa-65 branch hits the same near.getAccessKey\ndefense-in-depth as the ed25519 path, so the key still has to be a\nreal full-access key on the claimed account.\n\nAlso bumps near-kit ^0.14.0 -> ^0.19.0 so the RPC layer understands\nthe ml-dsa-65: and ml-dsa-65-hash: prefixes on getAccessKey. Bumps\nthe same range in the auth.everything.dev example catalog and extends\nsync-example-version.mjs to keep that catalog entry in lockstep with\nfuture parent-lib bumps.\n\n* fix: only notify $sessionSignal after a successful setPrimaryAccount; note near-kit 0.19 native deps","tree":{"sha":"8d2f5da2a00494a87d87961c385b07a5f2be636f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/trees/8d2f5da2a00494a87d87961c385b07a5f2be636f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/commits/442119f948aac5e298010d5491a70cea2ce23c54","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d2f5da2a00494a87d87961c385b07a5f2be636f\nparent 6a38d0ea22676c7ca7bd6aa1254455a0c48e8953\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1788400914 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788400914 -0500\n\nfeat: accept ml-dsa-65 NEP-413 signatures in SIWN verify endpoints (#77)\n\n* upgrade\n\n* feat: accept ml-dsa-65 NEP-413 signatures in SIWN verify endpoints\n\nWallets holding post-quantum ml-dsa-65: (FIPS 204) full-access keys are\nnow accepted by /api/auth/near/verify and /api/auth/near/link-account.\nPreviously the request bounced with 401 Unauthorized: Invalid signature\nbecause near-kit''s verifyNep413Signature hardcodes Ed25519.\n\nAdds a sibling verifyMlDsa65Nep413Signature helper that uses\n@noble/post-quantum''s ml_dsa65.verify, re-using the same NEP-413\nSHA-256 + borsh payload format and the same timestamp-based maxAge\ncheck. The ml-dsa-65 branch hits the same near.getAccessKey\ndefense-in-depth as the ed25519 path, so the key still has to be a\nreal full-access key on the claimed account.\n\nAlso bumps near-kit ^0.14.0 -> ^0.19.0 so the RPC layer understands\nthe ml-dsa-65: and ml-dsa-65-hash: prefixes on getAccessKey. Bumps\nthe same range in the auth.everything.dev example catalog and extends\nsync-example-version.mjs to keep that catalog entry in lockstep with\nfuture parent-lib bumps.\n\n* fix: only notify $sessionSignal after a successful setPrimaryAccount; note near-kit 0.19 native deps","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmNUSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkHMQAEv0Nn/xIqdNzKWZIZ8o2KW9\n2SU1tpQhX0Dg3+4Dz7SNPixXMYPZyT9z8+OycKoHpkK2SgrKIqdXU523IopVLTLK\n67UnhC7qDOUQmlz5jCMZErH5/QiuO/rkTfAYwVyrHH1NS6VBIwg9SqBjs7beWAD5\nco8VjghEB44cDpz85ahfTz3UxaTDm4QpDlJAjRRqJB7EnIkeTDIzi5vWez6Qpfb4\nyJI+iXmMV0+w3HJr8di2lOsFEE6wR1HllWymlISEB1IxMiJE/NBYYB1451p1o72F\n9bnYu64v++7J4DNVEzO21ocrUbGXLTwJMDzFFfJ6gIJrgZ3/+1axAuthidpLGZXa\n+EeSHqIdR12yZ1UcOH9rclr+BI4KNwAtjFN5s+QHV/H9f2lt95MNPbOFrusmSLRI\n6Zk1howzfvSaZLg85HTvON+bWyB74okkBFy+s8Qzfddex+m7GaAvdCg/2vg2s05K\nchD77Z4WmKV0WdQjMeoVyYXvVABWaAE5vsxeTDio7jrqWyCR05TXYxbKxDF+e7Ct\nGO9p5u7nUgJqJpk3Jv+qo4oiaP4RL+IejYscOhAspnlchjzSGjwBIYOYd1byeBer\nKy2VAzxhPbc4+T/CwuFnkoRPKxyoZ0fiXtJgjAo4Pr0dlJgkjqDgu9Xt2U2jNYZP\nSwKjs/3vDzXWTR+Qq7eY\n=MzKx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T02:01:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https: