in":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commit/0e4d02356dacaf563ff91d5112c80e1e1e878b7c","node_id":"C_kwDOPe0UwtoAKDBlNGQwMjM1NmRhY2FmNTYzZmY5MWQ1MTEyYzgwZTFlMWU4NzhiN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commit/4ea5aade0743d989c4a7351f2b3215780d299cc0","sha":"4ea5aade0743d989c4a7351f2b3215780d299cc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/4ea5aade0743d989c4a7351f2b3215780d299cc0"}],"sha":"0e4d02356dacaf563ff91d5112c80e1e1e878b7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/0e4d02356dacaf563ff91d5112c80e1e1e878b7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/commits/4ea5aade0743d989c4a7351f2b3215780d299cc0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:53:46Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:53:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: collapse relayer config into single shape with per-network secrets (#73)\n\n* fix drift\n\n* feat: collapse relayer config into single shape with per-network secrets\n\nMirror the subaccount config pattern: one flat per-network schema (no\nprivateKey, no privateKeys, no ephemeral: true marker, no true shorthand),\nalways dual-network shape, no isExplicitRelayerConfig type guard.\n\nSIWN library (`src/index.ts`):\n- Replace `RelayerEphemeralConfig | RelayerExplicitConfig | RelayerDualNetworkConfig | true` union\n  with a single flat `RelayerConfig` interface (accountId, privateKey,\n  whitelistedContracts, maxGasPerTransaction, maxDepositPerTransaction — all optional).\n- The mode is now determined at runtime by whether accountId is set.\n  Explicit = accountId + privateKey. Ephemeral = otherwise.\n- Remove `privateKeys` (the rotation-array field) entirely. `RotatingKeyStore` import dropped.\n- Update `SIWNPluginOptions.relayer` type to `RelayerConfig | RelayerDualNetworkConfig`.\n- Add a warning in `initRelayer` when accountId is set but privateKey is\n  missing. Without this, the user''s explicit intent disappeared silently\n  (the ''ephemeral doesn''t always show'' bug).\n- Remove all `as` casts in getRelayerConfig, getRawParentKey, and the\n  relay endpoint — the flat type narrows naturally with `in` and `typeof`.\n\nExample plugin (`examples/auth.everything.dev/plugins/auth`):\n- `config-schemas.ts`: keep only `relayerNetworkSchema` (flat, no privateKey).\n  Variables are always `{ mainnet?, testnet? }` — same shape as subAccount.\n- Replace `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY` with `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_MAINNET`\n  and `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_TESTNET`.\n- `auth-config.ts` / `auth-export.ts`: use `RelayerDualNetworkConfig` from\n  the library directly. Removed the artificial AuthRelayerEphemeralConfig /\n  AuthRelayerExplicitConfig / AuthRelayerDualNetworkConfig interfaces.\n- `config.ts`: `buildRelayerConfig` always returns a `RelayerDualNetworkConfig`\n  (or undefined). Private keys come exclusively from secrets — never from\n  variables. Throws a clear error if accountId is set but the corresponding\n  NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_{NETWORK} secret is missing (instead of silently\n  falling back to ephemeral).\n- `auth-instance.ts`: `buildSiwnOptions` no longer needs the artificial\n  isExplicitRelayerConfig guard — the validated config flows straight through.\n\nConfig files:\n- `plugin.dev.ts`, `bos.config.json`, `.env.example`: rename\n  NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY to per-network MAINNET/TESTNET variants.\n- Wrap the relayer in { mainnet: {...}, testnet: {...} } to match the new\n  dual-network shape.\n\nTests:\n- helpers.ts: MockBuilder is now generic over HandlerFn<R> so handler return\n  types propagate to test assertions. addTestMember''s role is typed as the\n  proper ''member'' | ''owner'' | ''admin'' union.\n- config.test.ts: rewritten to match the new dual-network format and\n  per-network secrets. Verifies fail-loud behavior when secret is missing.\n- api-keys.test.ts: drops the unused ''headers'' property from createTestApiKey calls.\n- near.test.ts: Sandbox type uses Awaited<ReturnType<typeof Sandbox.start>>,\n  Response casts go through unknown, and undefined array access is handled.\n\nAll 40 typecheck errors resolved. SIWN library: 61/61 tests pass.\nExample plugin: 171/171 tests pass.\n\n* Update relayer-simplify.md","tree":{"sha":"a84543b2c51369dd160d92710f0e4ff4a1ad766b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/trees/a84543b2c51369dd160d92710f0e4ff4a1ad766b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elliotBraem/better-near-auth/git/commits/4ea5aade0743d989c4a7351f2b3215780d299cc0","verification":{"payload":"tree a84543b2c51369dd160d92710f0e4ff4a1ad766b\nparent 1ae85e8ab1348c029aba2332132e5336cc425f5b\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1787090026 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787090026 -0500\n\nfeat: collapse relayer config into single shape with per-network secrets (#73)\n\n* fix drift\n\n* feat: collapse relayer config into single shape with per-network secrets\n\nMirror the subaccount config pattern: one flat per-network schema (no\nprivateKey, no privateKeys, no ephemeral: true marker, no true shorthand),\nalways dual-network shape, no isExplicitRelayerConfig type guard.\n\nSIWN library (`src/index.ts`):\n- Replace `RelayerEphemeralConfig | RelayerExplicitConfig | RelayerDualNetworkConfig | true` union\n  with a single flat `RelayerConfig` interface (accountId, privateKey,\n  whitelistedContracts, maxGasPerTransaction, maxDepositPerTransaction — all optional).\n- The mode is now determined at runtime by whether accountId is set.\n  Explicit = accountId + privateKey. Ephemeral = otherwise.\n- Remove `privateKeys` (the rotation-array field) entirely. `RotatingKeyStore` import dropped.\n- Update `SIWNPluginOptions.relayer` type to `RelayerConfig | RelayerDualNetworkConfig`.\n- Add a warning in `initRelayer` when accountId is set but privateKey is\n  missing. Without this, the user''s explicit intent disappeared silently\n  (the ''ephemeral doesn''t always show'' bug).\n- Remove all `as` casts in getRelayerConfig, getRawParentKey, and the\n  relay endpoint — the flat type narrows naturally with `in` and `typeof`.\n\nExample plugin (`examples/auth.everything.dev/plugins/auth`):\n- `config-schemas.ts`: keep only `relayerNetworkSchema` (flat, no privateKey).\n  Variables are always `{ mainnet?, testnet? }` — same shape as subAccount.\n- Replace `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY` with `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_MAINNET`\n  and `NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_TESTNET`.\n- `auth-config.ts` / `auth-export.ts`: use `RelayerDualNetworkConfig` from\n  the library directly. Removed the artificial AuthRelayerEphemeralConfig /\n  AuthRelayerExplicitConfig / AuthRelayerDualNetworkConfig interfaces.\n- `config.ts`: `buildRelayerConfig` always returns a `RelayerDualNetworkConfig`\n  (or undefined). Private keys come exclusively from secrets — never from\n  variables. Throws a clear error if accountId is set but the corresponding\n  NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY_{NETWORK} secret is missing (instead of silently\n  falling back to ephemeral).\n- `auth-instance.ts`: `buildSiwnOptions` no longer needs the artificial\n  isExplicitRelayerConfig guard — the validated config flows straight through.\n\nConfig files:\n- `plugin.dev.ts`, `bos.config.json`, `.env.example`: rename\n  NEAR_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY to per-network MAINNET/TESTNET variants.\n- Wrap the relayer in { mainnet: {...}, testnet: {...} } to match the new\n  dual-network shape.\n\nTests:\n- helpers.ts: MockBuilder is now generic over HandlerFn<R> so handler return\n  types propagate to test assertions. addTestMember''s role is typed as the\n  proper ''member'' | ''owner'' | ''admin'' union.\n- config.test.ts: rewritten to match the new dual-network format and\n  per-network secrets. Verifies fail-loud behavior when secret is missing.\n- api-keys.test.ts: drops the unused ''headers'' property from createTestApiKey calls.\n- near.test.ts: Sandbox type uses Awaited<ReturnType<typeof Sandbox.start>>,\n  Response casts go through unknown, and undefined array access is handled.\n\nAll 40 typecheck errors resolved. SIWN library: 61/61 tests pass.\nExample plugin: 171/171 tests pass.\n\n* Update relayer-simplify.md","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhNRqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsrgQAAQY77t6u9X2mLfvaaGDyhMb\nKV593qzP8GkMHxBrbxCxgGk7L/M69idJgV2M2QbdHGKKjJk/MtSqwiF+H