rm8/commits/6cbde92a0ee1c8d04649ce2d098e242f777dbe8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-16T16:58:14Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-16T16:58:14Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"Feat: Initial Repository Setup and Documentation\n\nThis pull request addresses the initial setup of the ArkoCRM repository for local development without Docker. It also adds important documentation and guardrails to help new developers get started quickly.\n\nWhat Changed and Why\n\n- `.gitignore`: A `.gitignore` file was added to prevent generated files, dependencies, and sensitive information (like `.env` files and `vendor` directory) from being committed to the repository. This is a standard best practice for Composer-based projects. Several previously tracked directories (`logs`, `.env`, `public/bundles`) were also untracked.\n- `.env.example`: An `.env.example` file was created to provide a clear template for the necessary environment variables. This allows developers to set up their local environment without having to guess the required configuration.\n- `README.md`: The `README.md` was updated with a \"Local Development (no Docker)\" section. This provides step-by-step instructions for setting up and running the application locally, which is crucial for new contributors.\n- `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`: A `CONTRIBUTING.md` file was created to establish clear guidelines for contributions. This ensures that the project maintains a consistent and manageable codebase.\n\nPHP 8.2 Adjustments\n\nNo PHP 8.2 adjustments were made in the end. The initial plan was to ensure `composer install` works with PHP 8.2, but per your instruction, I skipped this step and used the existing `vendor` directory. The `composer.json` file was left in its original state.\n\nCode Review\n\nThe `request_code_review()` tool failed due to a \"Request payload size exceeds the limit\" error. This is an environment limitation, so I was unable to get a code review before submitting.\n\nLocal Run Steps\n\nTo run the application locally, follow these steps:\n\n1.  **Clone the repository.**\n2.  **Configure your environment:**\n    ```bash\n    cp .env.example .env\n    ```\n    Edit the `.env` file to configure your `DATABASE_URL` and `SITE_URL`.\n3.  **Run the application:**\n    ```bash\n    php -S localhost:8000 -t public\n    ```\n    Access the application at `http://localhost:8000`.","tree":{"sha":"a7ed3318f4a9ffddfcf10035a8db95c190d21418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sarapil/suitecrm8/git/trees/a7ed3318f4a9ffddfcf10035a8db95c190d21418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sarapil/suitecrm8/git/commits/6cbde92a0ee1c8d04649ce2d098e242f777dbe8b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/842251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/google-labs-jules","id":161369871,"login":"google-labs-jules[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDOCZ5PDw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions