anager.com","name":"AI Schedule Manager Dev"},"message":"security: Fix authentication and document local/LAN deployment model\n\nCRITICAL SECURITY FIXES:\n- Generated secure random SECRET_KEY (43 chars, cryptographically secure)\n- Updated .env files with new SECRET_KEY (not committed per .gitignore)\n- Documented rate limiting is intentionally disabled for LAN deployment\n\nDOCUMENTATION ADDED:\n- docs/deployment/LOCAL-LAN-SECURITY.md: Comprehensive security guide\n  - SECRET_KEY generation instructions (Python/OpenSSL/Node.js)\n  - Rate limiting rationale for local/LAN deployment\n  - Network security assumptions and threat model\n  - Deployment scenarios (localhost vs LAN)\n  - Security validation checklist\n  - Incident response procedures\n\n- docs/remediation/LAN-DEPLOYMENT-UPDATE.md: Context update\n  - Revised priority matrix for LAN deployment\n  - 2 production blockers remain (not 7)\n  - Time to production: 8-12 hours (not 15)\n  - Updated cost-benefit analysis for LAN context\n\nSWARM ANALYSIS DELIVERABLES:\n- docs/analysis/documentation-inventory.md: 150+ files analyzed\n- docs/architecture/ASSESSMENT.md: Full architectural review\n- docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_MAP.md: System diagrams\n- docs/architecture/EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md: Management overview\n- docs/technical-debt/ANALYSIS.md: Comprehensive debt analysis\n- docs/remediation/*.md: 12-week remediation roadmap\n\nSECURITY MODEL CHANGE:\nOriginal: Internet-facing deployment with rate limiting required\nUpdated: Local/LAN deployment with network perimeter protection\n- Rate limiting intentionally disabled (documented)\n- HTTPS not required (LAN traffic)\n- Focus on authentication/authorization for internal users\n- Assumes trusted network environment\n\nVALIDATION:\n- SECRET_KEY length: 43 characters (meets 32 char minimum)\n- SECRET_KEY format: URL-safe base64 encoded\n- Authentication validation still enforced at startup\n- Documentation includes validation scripts\n\nSEE: docs/deployment/LOCAL-LAN