ixing async SQLAlchemy lazy loading issues:\n   - Added eager loading with selectinload() for roles relationship\n   - Added nested eager loading for role permissions\n   - Fixed User.to_dict() which triggered lazy loading of roles/permissions\n   - Updated all auth endpoints (register, login, refresh, get_current_user)\n   - Converted all database queries to use async/await patterns\n\nChanges:\n- backend/migrations/versions/003_add_auth_tables.py (new)\n- backend/src/main.py (auth service initialization)\n- backend/src/auth/fastapi_routes.py (async queries with eager loading)\n\nTested:\n- Registration endpoint: Successfully creates users\n- Login endpoint: Successfully authenticates users\n- Get current user endpoint: Returns user data without errors\n- Authentication loop: Resolved (no more 401/400/200 cycles)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Update demo login credentials to match backend requirements\n\nThe frontend was trying to login with ''demo123'' which is too short\n(minimum 8 characters required by backend). This caused a rapid\nreload loop as authentication kept failing.\n\nChanges:\n- Updated demo password from ''demo123'' to ''Demo123!'' (meets requirements)\n- Created demo user account in database with proper credentials\n- Frontend now successfully authenticates with demo account\n\nThe reload loop was caused by:\n1. Demo login failing with invalid credentials\n2. Auth context detecting failed login\n3. Redirecting to login page\n4. User clicking demo again\n5. Loop repeating rapidly\n\nDemo credentials:\n- Email: demo@example.com\n- Password: Demo123!\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Prevent reload loops during auth initialization\n\nFixed rapid page reload issue during hard refresh by:\n\n1. Added initialization guard with useRef to prevent multiple\n   simultaneous auth initialization calls\n\n2. Improved error handling for network errors:\n   - ECONNABORTED errors are now handled gracefully\n   - Network errors show debug messages instead of warnings\n   - Prevents error spam in console during network delays\n\n3. Added try-catch around CSRF token fetch to prevent failures\n   from breaking the entire auth flow\n\nThe reload loop was caused by:\n- Hard refresh triggering multiple auth initializations\n- Network requests being aborted during rapid reloads\n- Errors causing immediate logout and re-initialization\n- Cycle repeating indefinitely causing flickering\n\nChanges:\n- frontend/src/contexts/AuthContext.jsx (initializeAuth function)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Stop infinite reload loop on login/register pages\n\nThe reload loop was caused by the axios interceptor redirecting\nto /login when already on /login, causing an infinite loop.\n\nRoot cause analysis:\n1. User lands on /login page (no auth tokens)\n2. AuthContext tries to initialize auth by calling /api/auth/me\n3. Backend returns 401 (no token)\n4. Axios interceptor tries to refresh token\n5. Refresh fails (no refresh token cookie)\n6. Interceptor calls window.location.href = ''/login''\n7. Page reloads, goto step 1 - INFINITE LOOP\n\nFixes applied:\n1. AuthContext now skips initialization on /login and /register pages\n   - No point checking auth when user is trying to authenticate\n\n2. Axios interceptor checks current path before redirect\n   - Only redirects to /login if NOT already on /login or /register\n   - Prevents the reload loop completely\n\nResult: Login page now loads cleanly without reload loops\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Add missing department relationships to Employee and Shift models\n\n- Added department_id foreign key and department relationship to