e frontend and backend Docker deployment\n\nFixed all dependency issues and container deployment:\n\nFrontend fixes:\n- Upgraded date-fns from v2.30.0 to v3.6.0 for @mui/x-date-pickers compatibility\n- Fixed CheckCircle icon imports from @mui/material to @mui/icons-material\n- Fixed import ordering violations in App.jsx and SchedulePage.jsx\n- Changed useOnlineStatus to default export\n- Successfully built production React bundle\n\nBackend fixes:\n- Added missing cachetools==5.3.2 dependency\n- Fixed DATABASE_URL to use postgresql+asyncpg:// for async SQLAlchemy\n\nDocker deployment:\n- All three containers (postgres, backend, frontend) now running\n- Database: PostgreSQL 15 (healthy)\n- Backend: FastAPI with async database (healthy)\n- Frontend: React + Nginx production build (healthy)\n- Health checks passing for all services\n\nTested endpoints:\n- Frontend: http://localhost/ (200 OK)\n- Frontend health: http://localhost/health (healthy)\n- Backend health: http://localhost:8000/health (healthy)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Add Redis container for authentication token management\n\nAdded Redis to docker-compose for session/token storage:\n- Redis 7-alpine container with health check\n- Backend now depends on both postgres and redis\n- Added REDIS_URL environment variable to backend config\n- Fixed demo account login functionality\n\nThis resolves \"Refresh token generation failed\" errors.\n\nDemo credentials (not committed to git, update .env manually):\n- POSTGRES_DB=ai_schedule_manager\n- POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres\n\nTest account:\n- Email: testdemo@example.com\n- Password: Demo@123456\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Resolve nginx 502 Bad Gateway for API proxy\n\nFixed nginx proxy configuration issues:\n\n1. Added Docker DNS resolver (127.0.0.11) for container name resolution\n2. Changed proxy_pass to use variable with container name\n   - From: http://backend:8000 (cached DNS)\n   - To: http://ai-schedule-backend:8000 (dynamic resolution)\n\nRoot cause: Nginx was caching DNS resolution and connecting to\nthe wrong container (Redis instead of Backend).\n\nSolution: Using nginx variable forces DNS re-resolution on each\nrequest using Docker''s internal DNS resolver.\n\nTested: Login now works successfully through web interface\n✅ POST /api/auth/login returns JWT token\n✅ Frontend → Nginx → Backend communication working\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: Update hasRole to support both string and array parameters\n\n- AuthContext hasRole now accepts both single string and array of roles\n- Layout component passes array of required roles (e.g., [''admin'', ''manager''])\n- This enables proper role-based filtering of navigation menu items\n- Admin pages (Departments, Shifts, Roles, Employees) now visible to users with correct roles\n\n* feat: Implement critical security hardening fixes\n\n- Remove default SECRET_KEY from docker-compose.yml\n- Add SECRET_KEY validation requiring 32+ characters on startup\n- Implement API rate limiting with slowapi (5/min for login, 10/min for refresh, 5/hour for register)\n- Restrict CORS to specific origins and methods\n- Add comprehensive security headers to nginx (X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy)\n- Configure Docker backend to run as non-root user\n- Create .env.example with security documentation\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Switch from demo mode to real JWT authentication\n\n- Replace demo user with actual JWT token validation\n- Extract and verify Bearer token from Authorization header\n- Query user from database using token payload\n- Check user is_active and account lock status\n- Add proper